+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011VubALL6vbochs79xisfit","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is working. Here's a summary of what I built.\n\n## Summary\n\nA reactive spreadsheet engine in TypeScript, organized into focused modules under `src/`:\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| `references.ts` | Cell-ref ↔ coordinate conversion (multi-letter columns `A`→`AA`→…), range expansion (column, row, and 2D block) |\n| `tokenizer.ts` | Lexer for formula expressions (numbers incl. scientific notation, strings, operators, refs) |\n| `ast.ts` | AST node type definitions |\n| `parser.ts` | Recursive-descent parser with correct operator precedence (comparison → additive → multiplicative → unary → primary) |\n| `evaluator.ts` | Dependency collection + AST evaluation, built-in functions, type coercion, error codes |\n| `index.ts` | The `Spreadsheet` class: storage, dependency graph, cycle detection, reactive recomputation |\n\n### Key design points\n\n- **Reactivity**: a reverse-dependency index (`dependents`) lets `set()` find all transitively affected cells, which are then recomputed in **topological order** (Kahn's algorithm) so each cell sees fresh upstream values — a diamond dependency recomputes each node exactly once.\n- **Circular reference detection**: before committing a formula, a DFS from its dependencies checks whether the target cell is reachable. If so it throws `CircularReferenceError` and **leaves the spreadsheet unchanged** (the check runs pre-commit).\n- **Error semantics**: division by zero → `#DIV/0!`, non-numeric arithmetic → `#VALUE!`, unparseable formulas → `#ERROR!`. Errors **propagate** to dependents and **recover** automatically when the source is fixed.\n- **Functions**: `SUM`, `AVERAGE`, `MIN`, `MAX`, `COUNT` (ignore non-numeric cells in ranges), and `IF` with all six comparison operators (`> < >= <= = <>`), including nesting.\n- **Niceties**: case-insensitive refs, empty cells treated as 0 in arithmetic (and reactive once filled), float-noise trimming in `getDisplay` (`=0.1+0.2` → `\"0.3\"`), `TRUE`/`FALSE` display formatting.\n\n### Verification\n- ✅ **40 tests pass** (`npm test`) covering all documented examples plus edge cases\n- ✅ **Lint clean** (`npm run lint`)\n- ✅ **Builds** (`npm run build`) — test files excluded from the published `dist/`\n\nThe exact examples from the spec (`A3=30`→`70` on reactive update, `SUM(A1:A2)=70`, `IF(A1>30,\"big\",\"small\")`) are all exercised in the test suite."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":54529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":355},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feca5c43-c310-47f9-a074-12cc1a72d3fb","uuid":"1127c086-e670-4789-ad9b-0b57f90997c1","request_id":"req_011CcBFTrbN9dCAq56numi6c"}
